      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T15:29:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the intended plan for the capture manager state when getCapture() is called? Do we want this to be more like a \"snap\" where the returned capture represents everything collected up to this point and then the manager is reset?\n\nOr should it just return a capture holding everything since capture was toggled on.  If capturing remains enabled, new data gets appended a future call to getCapture() returns a new object that contains the same initial picture data and anything added later.  We would reset only when capturing was toggled off?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "4f9b9ee781088c83ca7302c7f7a78f3f90af950a",
